{# Backslashes are doubled throughout: Jinja unescapes string literals, so '\1' is chr(1). #}
{% set root_fs = (ansible_mounts | selectattr('mount', 'equalto', '/') | list | first) | default({}, true) %}
{# mokutil answers on stderr where the firmware has no Secure Boot support at all. #}
{% set secure_boot = ((report_secure_boot.stdout | default('', true)) ~ (report_secure_boot.stderr | default('', true))) | trim %}
{% set kernel_candidate = (report_signed_kernel.stdout | regex_search('Candidate:\\s*(\\S+)', '\\1') or ['not offered by apt'])[0] %}
{% set spbm_loaded = 'spbm' in (report_modules.stdout | default('', true)) %}
{% set hwmon = report_hwmon.stdout | default('', true) | trim %}
{% set power_channels = report_power_channels.stdout | default('', true) | trim %}
{% set firmware = report_firmware.stdout | default('', true) | trim %}
================================================================================
 sparkup report for {{ inventory_hostname }}. Nothing on this box was changed.
================================================================================

WILL THIS REPO RUN HERE
{% if 'SecureBoot enabled' in secure_boot %}
  Secure Boot          enabled
{% elif report_secure_boot.rc is not defined %}
  Secure Boot          cannot be read here: mokutil is not installed
                       The converge installs it and checks before touching
                       anything, so this is not a blocker, only unknown for now.
{% else %}
  Secure Boot          {{ secure_boot or 'mokutil said nothing' }}
                       The converge REFUSES to start without it, before changing
                       anything. Re-enable it in firmware, or use another recipe.
{% endif %}
  Signed kernel        {{ kernel_candidate }}
{% if 'not offered' in kernel_candidate or kernel_candidate == '(none)' %}
                       linux-image-nvidia-hwe-24.04 is what the kernel role
                       boots. Without it this is not a DGX OS base and the
                       converge fails late, at apt.
{% endif %}

MACHINE
  Product              {{ ansible_product_name | default('?', true) }} / {{ ansible_board_name | default('?', true) }}
  BIOS                 {{ ansible_bios_version | default('?', true) }} ({{ ansible_bios_date | default('?', true) }})
  OS                   {{ ansible_distribution | default('?', true) }} {{ ansible_distribution_version | default('', true) }}
  DGX release          {{ (report_dgx_release.content | default('', true) | b64decode | trim) or 'no /etc/dgx-release' }}
  Kernel               {{ ansible_kernel | default('?', true) }} ({{ ansible_architecture | default('?', true) }})
  Memory               {{ ansible_memtotal_mb | default(0, true) }} MB
{% if root_fs.size_total | default(0) > 0 %}
  Root filesystem      {{ (root_fs.size_available / 1024 ** 3) | round | int }} GB free of {{ (root_fs.size_total / 1024 ** 3) | round | int }} GB
{% endif %}
  Uptime               {{ ((ansible_uptime_seconds | default(0)) / 3600) | round(1) }} h

GPU
{% if report_gpu.rc | default(1) == 0 %}
{{ report_gpu.stdout | default('', true) | trim | indent(4, true) }}
    (name, driver, compute capability, memory.total, power.draw, power.limit)
{% else %}
    nvidia-smi did not answer: {{ (report_gpu.stderr | default('', true)) | trim or (report_gpu.msg | default('unknown error', true)) }}
{% endif %}

WHOLE-SYSTEM POWER
  spbm module          {{ 'loaded' if spbm_loaded else 'not loaded (the default; the dashboard Power row stays empty)' }}
  hwmon devices
{% if hwmon %}
{{ hwmon | indent(4, true) }}
{% else %}
    none
{% endif %}
{% if power_channels %}
  power channels
{{ power_channels | indent(4, true) }}
{% endif %}

CLAIMS THIS REPO MAKES, WHICH YOUR BOX EITHER CONFIRMS OR KILLS
Most of these were measured on one machine on one day. Where yours disagrees,
reality wins and the docs are wrong: please open a "Hardware finding" issue.

{# No `true` on these defaults: it would treat a perfectly good rc of 0 as missing. #}
  no readable RTC      timedatectl exits {{ report_timedatectl.rc | default('nothing, it is not installed') }}   (claimed: non-zero, EFI RTC reads fail)
  SSH socket-activated {% for unit in report_ssh_units.results | default([], true) %}{{ unit.item }} {{ unit.status.UnitFileState | default('absent', true) }}{{ ' / ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}   (claimed: ssh.socket enabled, ssh.service disabled)
  hidden boot menu     /etc/default/grub.d/no-grubmenu.cfg {{ 'present' if report_grub_dropin.stat.exists else 'ABSENT' }}   (claimed: present, forcing GRUB_TIMEOUT=0)
  unified GPU memory   see memory.total above   (claimed: [N/A], the field is dropped)

FIRMWARE
Older EC firmware reports incorrect CPU power. The converge stages what fwupd
offers and never reboots; the versions below are what this box runs today.

{% if firmware %}
{{ firmware | indent(2, true) }}
{% else %}
  fwupdmgr did not answer: {{ (report_firmware.stderr | default('', true)) | trim or (report_firmware.msg | default('unknown error', true)) }}
{% endif %}
